# SRG-APP-000516-WSR-000174  -  CAT II
# The web server must be configured in accordance with the security
# configuration settings based on DoD security configuration or
# implementation guidance, including STIGs, NSA configuration guides, CTOs,
# and DTMs.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000516-WSR-000174
group:           V-206445
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-000366
control_rev5:    CM-6

contribution:    The application can hold the two concrete settings the benchmark authority
                 states for this product, and can carry the rest of the applicable guidance
                 as explicit values in its own .conf files rather than relying on shipped
                 defaults.

governs:         server.conf - Core server settings, including the certificates and protocols used to
                 protect management and replication traffic.
governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           web.conf [settings] enableSplunkWebSSL in true|1
check:           server.conf [sslConfig] enableSplunkdSSL in true|1
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          server.conf [sslConfig] enableSplunkdSSL https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.4/secure-splunk-platform-communications-with-transport-layer-security-certificates/configure-tls-certificates-for-inter-splunk-communication
vendor:          web.conf [settings] enableSplunkWebSSL https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The rest of this requirement is the sum of the other rules in this
                 checklist: it has no setting of its own beyond the values the product STIG
                 states, and the check inventory attaches whole .conf files to it rather
                 than a key.
external:        Which guidance applies - the STIGs, NSA configuration guides, CTOs, and
                 DTMs in scope - is an organizational determination, and the operating
                 system, network, and procedural portions of those documents are carried
                 outside the application.
external:        Precedence matters when reading the result: a value in the system-local
                 layer outranks the hardening app, so guidance delivered as an app can be
                 overridden on the host.

citation:        SPLK-CL-000290 check and fix text; Web Server SRG
                 SRG-APP-000516-WSR-000174 check text; web.conf.spec:70
                 (enableSplunkWebSSL, default false), server.conf.spec:724
                 (enableSplunkdSSL)
finding:         The settings the benchmark authority states for this product are not
                 configured, so the application is not configured in accordance with the
                 security configuration guidance that applies to it.
